Early modern and modern world history (@early-modern-and-modern-world-history: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_27AZJWR6C6Y5DVRSDA9SSWKEQH
This material follows transformations in states, economies, belief, knowledge, and everyday life from early modern contexts into the modern world. It connects empires, colonial systems, trade, political revolutions, industrialisation, labour, scientific change, and contested forms of citizenship. Compare regional histories and competing explanations using evidence at the appropriate scale. Link Political-Economy, Sociology, Philosophy, and Literature so that institutions and ideas remain connected to the people and material arrangements through which they changed.

